OpenBSD builders need more than the upstream 90-second per-example
watchdog for the complete asynchronous chat integration workloads. Keep
every test and assertion intact while retaining a finite cleanup-safe
bound.

getProfilePictureByName must not assume the profile image has already
been delivered: poll for a bounded time and decode the nullable column
as Maybe, so a late update returns Nothing instead of failing with a
NULL-to-Text conversion error.

Independent member connections have no defined completion order. Assert
both.

The (<??) operator consumes up to N optional asynchronous lines and
fails on any other output, so the examples below can account for the
member-connected group items without weakening their assertions.

